aragraph></ListItem></List><Paragraph FontFamily="Calibri" FontSize="14.666666666666666" Margin="0,0,0,0.93"><Span><Run>Medium Impact BES Cyber Systems with External Routable Connectivity and their associated: </Run></Span></Paragraph><List MarkerStyle="Decimal" Margin="0,0,0,0" Padding="0,0,0,0"><ListItem Margin="48,0,0,0"><Paragraph FontFamily="Calibri" FontSize="14.666666666666666" Margin="0,0,0,2.47"><Span><Run>EACMS; and</Run></Span></Paragraph></ListItem><ListItem Margin="48,0,0,0"><Paragraph FontFamily="Calibri" FontSize="14.666666666666666" Margin="0,0,0,0"><Span><Run>PACS</Run></Span></Paragraph></ListItem></List></TableCell><TableCell Padding="6.4,7.47,1.4,0" BorderThickness="1,1,1,1" BorderBrush="#FF000000"><Paragraph FontFamily="Calibri" FontSize="14.666666666666666" Margin="0.8,0,0,0"><Span><Run>Require completion of the training specified in Part 2.1 prior to granting authorized electronic access and authorized unescorted physical access to applicable Cyber Assets, except during CIP Exceptional Circumstances.  </Run></Span></Paragraph></TableCell><TableCell Padding="6.4,7.47,1.4,0" BorderThickness="1,1,1,1" BorderBrush="#FF000000"><Paragraph FontFamily="Calibri" FontSize="14.666666666666666" Margin="1.8,0,0,0"><Span><Run>Examples of evidence may include, but are not limited to, training records and documentation of when CIP Exceptional Circumstances were invoked. </Run></Span></Paragraph></TableCell></TableRow><TableRow><TableCell Padding="6.4,7.47,1.4,0" BorderThickness="1,1,1,1" BorderBrush="#FF000000"><Paragraph FontFamily="Calibri" FontSize="14.666666666666666" Margin="0.73,0,0,0"><Span><Run>2.3 </Run></Span></Paragraph></TableCell><TableCell Padding="6.4,7.47,1.4,0" BorderThickness="1,1,1,1" BorderBrush="#FF000000"><Paragraph FontFamily="Calibri" FontSize="14.666666666666666" Margin="0,0,0,0.87"><Span><Run>High Impact BES Cyber Systems and their associated: </Run></Span></Paragraph><List MarkerStyle="Decimal" Margin="0,0,0,0" Padding="0,0,0,0"><Li